.TH TESTIFEX 1 "October 2026" "TESTIFEX 0.1.0a1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
testifex \- compatibility command for earlier evidence cases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B testifex
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is the earlier case-format command supplied with PROBENTIUM.
It maintains supported evidence timelines with explicit time uncertainty.
Its commands and case format differ from the current probentium command;
it is not an alias for that command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
testifex init legacy-case \-\-name "Legacy exercise"
testifex ingest \-\-case legacy-case evidence.jsonl \\
  \-\-format events \-\-label "Synthetic input"
testifex timeline \-\-case legacy-case
testifex verify \-\-case legacy-case
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help for the selected command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH COMMANDS
init, ingest, resume, sources, issues, timeline, event, analyze, report,
snapshot, share, triage, diff, verify, replay, hypothesis, browse and demo.
.PP
Consult command-specific help before applying operations to an existing case.
For current functionality and documented migration, use probentium.
.SH SECURITY
Cases contain plaintext evidence. Byte verification does not prove authorship,
factual truth, legal compliance or collection completeness.
Use synthetic data when reporting bugs publicly.
.SH AUTHOR
Artifex Ignotvs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR probentium (1)
